1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,000
After we freeze this tight top coat, we will see that other versions can participate in the simulation, but the frozen version is not involved in the simulation and its shape will not change.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
The sewing line is still effective.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Then go to the tool bar of 2D and find the rectangular tool. In the window of 2D, click and drag it to about three times the width of the virtual model's waist.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Then use the adjustment panel tool to adjust to the appropriate width as needed. Then press Ctrl D to create a symmetrical panel.

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:47,000
In the window of 2D, move the panel and press Shift F to open the arrangement point. Arrange these two panels on the two arrangement points of the waist.

6
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
After the panel is aligned,

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
we go to the 2D window and use the line sewing tool.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Click on the two lines in the front to complete the sewing line, and then click on the two lines in the back to complete the sewing line.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
After opening the simulation by pressing Ctrl D, we will see that this panel is now on the virtual model.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
If the belt is relatively loose, you can adjust it manually.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Then we can activate the panels that were frozen by us before.

12
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Because it is now worn in the belt.

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
In the case that it is now stable,

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,000
we can gradually adjust it.

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,000
The tail-swing rate that was previously reduced returns to 100 little by little.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Note that do not return too much in one go.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Otherwise, it may cause instability due to too many adjustments in one go.

18
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Of course, if you choose to make the inner skirt as a whole,

19
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
you can finish the whole skirt first and then add the belt outside.

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Then we freeze the belt belt part that has been done, and also freeze the top part.

21
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Here we freeze these panels in order to maintain their current shape.

22
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
And when the panels are frozen, the software runs faster.

23
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
In order to facilitate our manual reference,

24
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
how long is the belt to be made later,

25
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
we first move the belt to the waist near the waist in the 2D simulation.

26
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Then we make a rectangular panel according to the 2D simulation,

27
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
as its shoulder strap.

28
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Note that because the human body is a three-dimensional model,

29
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
it is not a flat surface.

30
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
So when we draw the shoulder strap,

31
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
we have to make a long section.

32
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
This way, we have finished the strap on the front of the right side.

33
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Then we copy and paste a panel.

34
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Then press Ctrl D to create a total of four panels.

35
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
So now we have two pairs of shoulder straps corresponding to each other.

36
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Then press Shift F to open the arrangement point.

37
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
We arrange the front of this bag.

38
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
After arranging, go to the property editor.

39
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Arrange the position of the x-axis under the column.

40
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
You can adjust the position of the arrangement in the horizontal direction.

41
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
We put it closer to the center of the body.

42
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
The same goes for the back.

43
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,000
After arranging the appropriate arrangement point,

44
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
adjust the position of the x-axis.

45
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Let it be closer to the center of the body.

46
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Then we are going to start sewing.

47
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
If it is inconvenient to sew in the 2D window,

48
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
we might as well use the sewing tool in the 3D window.

49
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
It's the same as sewing in the 2D window.

50
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Click on a section of the line and then click on another section of the line.

51
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Note that the sewing lines do not cross.

52
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Then it's the bottom part.

53
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Here we are going to use free sewing.

54
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Because we are sewing a whole section of the panel

55
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
and a small section of the line on a panel,

56
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:36,000
so we have to use free sewing.

57
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
The back is the same.

58
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Then let's take a look at the free sewing in the 3D window.

59
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Click on it.

60
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Double click to complete the selection.

61
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Then click on the belt.

62
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Double click to complete the selection.

63
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
You can also do free sewing.

64
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Then we can simulate by pressing the control button.

65
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
After opening the simulation,

66
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
we will see that its shoulder strap is a little out of place.

67
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Then we press the control button to pause the simulation.

68
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Then press Ctrl Z to return to the time when the simulation has not started.

69
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
First, we press the control button to open the simulation.

70
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
After opening the simulation, we will see that

71
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
its shoulder strap is OK.

72
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
In order to prevent it from slipping,

73
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
we press the W key and click on the panel.

74
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
You can create a fixed stitch on the panel.

75
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
This way, the panel will not slip down.

76
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Then use the edge sewing line tool

77
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,000
to drag the sewing line in the belt here.

78
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
This way, the sewing line moves a little inward.

79
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
At this time, after we open the simulation,

80
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,000
the shoulder strap is more straight.

81
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Press the W key and click on the fixed stitch.

82
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
You can cancel the fixed stitch.

83
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
At this time, we will simulate

84
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
whether it can be fixed while dragging the shoulder strap.

85
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,000
In order to prevent it from moving,

86
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
we can use the tool on the virtual model.

87
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Click on the panel and then click on the virtual model.

88
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
In this way, we can sew the point on the panel

89
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
and the point on the virtual model together.

90
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
After opening the simulation,

91
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
if the shoulder strap is a little unnatural here,

92
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
we can find the edge sewing tool.

93
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
It is also in the previous download menu.

94
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
After selecting this edge sewing needle,

95
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
we can adjust the edge sewing tool

96
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:10,000
and adjust the length of the line.

97
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,000
When the length of the line is set to 2 mm,

98
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
there will be 2 mm of space between the two points.

99
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
In this way, it looks more natural.

100
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Let's look back.

101
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
The fixed needle is fixed in 3D space,

102
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
and the fake sewing needle virtual model

103
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
is connected to the virtual model.

104
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:31,000
After that, we can select all the panels and activate them.

105
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
At this time, if you see that the shoulder strap is a little long,

106
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
you can adjust it again in 2D space.

107
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Be careful not to affect the position of the fake sewing needle.

108
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,000
If the panel is longer,

109
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
it may look more obvious.

110
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
How do we judge that the panel is short?

111
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
First of all, we can press Ctrl Z to return to just now,

112
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
when we haven't simulated the whole thing.

113
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Then, in the 3D window,

114
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
switch to the hardware image

115
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
or press the number key Alt 7 directly.

116
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
We can see the stretch on the panel.

117
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
The blue and green parts show that it is OK now.

118
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,000
But if there is a red part,

119
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
it means that this part is tight.

120
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
We may need to adjust the length of the shoulder strap

121
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
or the width of the belt.

122
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Because some part of the stretch

123
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
may be related to it.

124
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
It may also be related to the panel that is sewn with it.

125
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
We can adjust it all and try it.

126
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Then we can turn off the hardware image.

127
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Then we will adjust the width of the shoulder strap.

128
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
When we adjust it,

129
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
first of all,

130
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
we avoid adjusting it to the side with the seam allowance.

131
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
In the process of moving,

132
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,000
don't forget that the front and back pieces

133
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
must move side by side at the same time.

134
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
In this way,

135
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
we can ensure that the width is correct.

136
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Don't forget to press the Shift key.

137
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
You can choose more.

138
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Then, because we have adjusted the width of the shoulder strap,

139
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
but free sewing,

140
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
its sewing line will not be adjusted automatically.

141
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
So we have to use the editor sewing line tool

142
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
to select the edge of the sewing line on the panel.

143
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Drag this edge to the blue point.

144
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
This represents that the two lines of the sewing line are equal.

145
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
This blue point is our reference point.

146
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
After adjusting,

147
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
we can freeze it into some tape

148
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
to adjust other parts.

